Third Ascension!
Yay.

Slightly over a week I've been playing this, at one point I thought I
was gone, with only 1 turn left, so I saved it a didn't do anything
for days.

Playing as Arcs for a while, trying to make lotsa money from IDed gems
to buy protection. A game just a few before this was doing very well,
got 9 or so points of protection at a low level, went down in the mines

until he found a luckstone, and by sokoban had reflection and bag of
holding. Cannot quite remember what order they came in, I think I might

have found an early shiny shield, or a magic lamp. Anyway, whacking
away at various beasties, he, um, accidently killed his puppy in a
gas-spore related incedent. There goes all that protection. Oops. I
decided to go back and convert the minetown altar, get the money from
the priest, and buy protection somewhere else. Easy. Killed by a
captain of the guard, but left quite a bones file, with neutral
minetown altar, a nive set of armor (from memory I found a +3 elvish
mithril, plus some other +2 bits and pieces.)

I love the thought that the poor guy was doing quite well until he
killed a puppy.

So when another neutral Arc stumbles across a minetown with abandoned
temple, I thought 'this guy has a chance.' Since it was a while ago,
plenty of the details are foggy/gone (curse those mind flayers!) but
here goes.

>From the bones I had heaps and heaps of money (I really struggled to
stay unburdened at first, and wasn't about to leave the stash behind.
Silly, perhaps, but it did mean I was ruthless in whatever else I
carried) a decent set of armor, and two silver sabers. In short time
I upped my saber and twoweapon skills, and plodded along okay. The
only non-leather/non-elven cloak I had for ages (in fact, it's the
only one I remember seeing in the game) was invisibility, which was
handy.

Typically, I had reflection early (from the bones, I think) and
sokoban was also reflection. Didn't find a bag of holding in the wild
until the Valley of the Dead, and the first priest I saw was about
DL 16. Maybe lower. I did find a magic lamp in the bottom of the
mines somewhere, and wished up a bag. Smoky potions were confusion,
and the one I found and blessed gave another wish, for +3 GDSM.
Nothing much else of note, took a while (and a few !oGL) before I
could do the quest, which wasn't particularly hard. I kept the Orb
of Detection in my BoH at first.

I did set up a stash at two altars. Nabbed a few gifts, TrollBane,
FireBrand and DragonBane. The first two I got when trying for a nifty
weapon, and FB at +6/+7 (wavered a bit thanks to disenchanters) was
my primary for the rest of the game, with a +6/+7 silver saber in the
other hand. DragonBane appeared when I was making a little sacrifice to

see if it were safe to pray for water, rather later on. Worked on
enchant
armor and weapons, most things to +4/+5. Did get an elven cloak to +6,
after accidentally evaporating another. Found some Gauntlets of Power
(after I got the BoH, so not a huge help lugging around all that cash),

and wore elven boots at +6 the whole game.

Somewhere in here my armor started to disintegrate. Only occasionally
noticed, but my cloak, two sets of elvish mithril (and one dwarvish,
I think), and maybe my Shield of relfection at various points were
turned to dust by monsters. The Cloak, maybe some of the mithril might
have been in the quest, but this is the first time that this has
happened to me. Maybe once or twice before, but this many times in one
game? Had me very worried. I figured it must be magic resistance or
magic cancellation related so carried the Orb outside the BoH for the
rest of the game (at least, when I could keep it at all.)

Medusa was the titan level, again. Dropped down and came up to get the
boots out of the statue, which lasted not very long before I IDed a
=3DoLevitation. Took ages trying to work out how to get into the castle.
No wands of opening. I guess I could have used striking/cold, but
either
didn't have wands, or didn't think of it then. Scoured the entire
dungeon and mines looking for a musical intrument. None. One drum, and
plenty of bugles, none of which I could play a tune on. (Ironically,
when I prayed one last time before the final run, just for luck and
roleplaying, I heard the tune. Still hadn't seen an instrument.) I did
find enough scrolls of id to get the ring, and Id a bunch of other
stuff.
Also cleared out Ludios while I was looking around. Around the back it
was. Cleared out the castle, already had a blessed charging scroll, so
first three wishes went to magic markers. Also got a blessed helm of
brilliance, 2 blessed scrolls of genocide for emergencys (never saw one

apart from that,) and a shirt. Tried once for Grayswandir, and felt
something for a moment. Two many artifacts, right. Oh well. Uncursed
the robe from minetown and enchanted it up to +4, and then went around
learning spells. Had a list from a-o pretty quick, and most easy to
cast with gloves off.

Wandered around Gehenom for a while, killing things, collecting stuff,
doing a little remodeling. By the time I killed Orcus, I had 4 wands of

death, which was nice. Especially with plenty of charging scrolls.
Killed Vlad and everything in his tower, and grabbed the Candelabrum
and "oLS. At one point there were a couple of Liches around, so I
genocided the lot. Had an accident or two with mind flayers, (geno'd
mmfs from a throne) and so wished up a book of magic mapping which made

life much easier. Eventually I was about L18, and decided to take on
the Wizard. I'd found the Vibrating Square, dumped everything I didn't
need. All was fine until I took on the Wizard.

Happily hitting away, oh he is invisible, no worries. Double trouble,
fine fine, I'll just kill'em both. OH SHIT, I'VE ONLY GOT ONE HP
LEFT!!!!!
Save. Start breathing again. Reload and check inventory. My wands of
death and potions of full healing are in separate bags. Wearing
"oReflection, not "oLS. Save again. Think. Can't pray. Wizard isn't
about to give me a break if I used the E-word, even if I weren't
levitating.

Came back to the game almost a week later. If I die, I figure, I die.
Took of the "oReflection. Nothing kills me. Put on "oLS. Begins to
glow.
Take out /oDeath, !oFH. Kill wizard. Repeat. Realize I've been zapping
death rays about wily-nily without any source of reflection. Put
"oReflection back on.

Then I rearranged my inventory a bit. Made sure I always carried a /oD
with a few charges. Put 2!oFH and a b?oCharging in the bag with my
wands. Started killing things with magic missile. And paying attention
to HP.

After that the game was fairly easy. Had to re-map half the dungeon.
Suffered quite a bit at the hands of malignant auras; cursing rings,
weapons, gloves, and uncursing BoH at one stage. Found another marker
for more charging and remove curse scrolls. Noticed Vorpal Blade
lying in an Orcus graveyard, so grabbed it. Zapped the Wizard whenever
he appeared. Freaked out when the power went out for a minute, but
game restored fine. Learnt the Charm Monster spell, which was really
handy for getting around, being able to push past preciously
peaceful monsters. Plus, the purple worms and ants that were brief
pets in the sanctum were fun. Got the amulet, dropped by an altar
on the way up to let my god know I was on the way, stop on DL2 to
have a bath and make some more blank scrolls. Planes were easy with
the Orb. Left 10 full /oDigging on Earth, quite a few pet elementals
on Air and Fire (and some dragons here and there.) No breathing, so
waited around on Water. Used my other b?oGenocide to get rid on all ;,
just in case. Hadn't used conflict since the sanctum (pets), so me
and my angel (who seemed to have an amulet of reflection. Neat) had
some fun on Astral. Tried the left altar first, Famine died easy,
and then:






